dts: hubv3l: disable the audio DAIs, they squat on button and Thread pins

No audio device is fitted on this board - boot ends with "No soundcards
found" - but the TDM and SPDIF nodes still grab their pins, and on this
PCB those pins do other jobs:

  GPIOA_0  BUTN_USR_A0  user button    <- tdmc_mclk (mclk_a)
  GPIOA_3  DB_BOOT2     Thread boot    <- tdmc_pins (tdmc_fs)

The symptoms were a button the supervisor could never request (gpioinfo
showed GPIOA_0 as "kernel [used]" even though patch 1001 splits uart_A's
pinctrl to free it) and:

  pin GPIOA_3 already requested by ff642000.audiobus:tdmc;
  cannot claim for periphs-banks:440

Disabling tdma/tdmc/spdif releases GPIOA_0 and GPIOA_2..4 in one go, which
beats picking pin groups out of each node's pinctrl list and revisiting it
every time another of these pins turns out to be wired to something.

tdma only covers GPIOX_12..15 and collides with nothing today; it goes
along with the others because it is equally unused. spdif already carried
status = "okay", so that one is flipped rather than given a second
property.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-axg-thirdreality-hub-v3l.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-axg-thirdreality-hub-v3l.dts
@@ -564,6 +564,7 @@
 &audiobus {
 	tdma: tdma {
 		compatible = "amlogic, axg-snd-tdma";
+		status = "disabled";
 		#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
 		dai-tdm-lane-slot-mask-in = <1 0>;
 		dai-tdm-lane-slot-mask-out = <0 1>;
@@ -577,6 +578,7 @@
 
 	tdmc: tdmc {
 		compatible = "amlogic, axg-snd-tdmc";
+		status = "disabled";
 		#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
 		dai-tdm-lane-slot-mask-out = <1 0>;
 		dai-tdm-lane-slot-mask-in = <0 1>;
@@ -619,7 +621,7 @@
 		 * 7: "Enable:192K",
 		 */
 		auto_asrc = <3>;
-		status = "okay";
+		status = "disabled";
 	};
 
 	pdm: pdm {
